+### 1.6 Reversing the groups of a string — `patches/fixes/0004-subobjects-group-category-reversal.patch`
+
+Also in the second patch group, and also a send to `#f`. Metacat builds a rule clause of the form
+`(subobjects <GroupCtgy> <Opposite>)` on purpose (`rule-scout`, `rules.ss:637-641`), and it has its
+own English, "Reverse starting and ending points of all objects in ..." (`get-change-phrase`,
+`rules.ss:1881-1883`). But a BondFacet change is made only for scope `self`
+(`get-BondFacet-change`, `rules.ss:1054-1059`), so the transform of each subobject is a bare
+`(<GroupCtgy> <Opposite>)` with no BondFacet partner. `apply-transforms` (`rules.ss:1341-1350`) took the
+medium as `(2nd (assq plato-bond-facet transforms))`, which is `(cadr #f)` when there is none:
+"incorrect list structure #f" (`pqcd -> cbpo; tugh`, seed 1, at codelet 2390).
+
+- **`apply-transforms`** now takes the medium from the BondFacet transform when the object has one,
+  and otherwise from the object's own image (`(tell image 'get-bond-facet)`, `images.ss:145`), so
+  each group reverses along its own medium, letter category or length. `reverse-medium` already does
+  nothing for a letter image (`images.ss:241`).
+- **`same-dimension-as-GroupCtgy-medium?`** (`check-for-conflicts`) sent `get-bond-facet` to the
+  change's reference object, and a letter has no such message: "bad message" (`rules.ss:1049`),
+  reachable once the first crash is out of the way, with a letter among the subobjects. A letter has
+  no medium, so it now answers false for a letter.
+
+Both changes are written on the lines they replace, so that no line of `rules.ss` moves and the line numbers
+cited for it elsewhere (`apply-transforms` at `rules.ss:1341-1353`) stay true.
+
+**Effect on behaviour: none where it does not fire.** A transform list with a BondFacet entry takes
+the same branch as before, and the objects that reach the new branch always ended in an error.
+
